{"name":"Brown-Noser","hex":"#79512c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brown-noser","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who brown-noses (flatters or humors somebody in an obsequious manner for personal gain); one who sucks up; a bootlicker, dickrider, ass-kisser, sycophant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown-noser"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sycophancy","blocks":[{"text":"In modern English, sycophant denotes an insincere flatterer and refers to someone practising sycophancy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Frivolous_Fables_fox_and_raven.gif/330px-Frivolous_Fables_fox_and_raven.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sycophancy","wikidata":"Q772259"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Parc_de_Versailles%2C_Rond-Point_des_Philosophes%2C_Lysias%2C_Jean_Dedieu_inv1850n%C2%B09452_03.jpg/500px-Parc_de_Versailles%2C_Rond-Point_des_Philosophes%2C_Lysias%2C_Jean_Dedieu_inv1850n%C2%B09452_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Parc_de_Versailles%2C_Rond-Point_des_Philosophes%2C_Lysias%2C_Jean_Dedieu_inv1850n%C2%B09452_03.jpg/1280px-Parc_de_Versailles%2C_Rond-Point_des_Philosophes%2C_Lysias%2C_Jean_Dedieu_inv1850n%C2%B09452_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Parc_de_Versailles%2C_Rond-Point_des_Philosophes%2C_Lysias%2C_Jean_Dedieu_inv1850n%C2%B09452_03.jpg/500px-Parc_de_Versailles%2C_Rond-Point_des_Philosophes%2C_Lysias%2C_Jean_Dedieu_inv1850n%C2%B09452_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lysias, by the French sculptor Jean Dedieu (c. 1645–1727)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParc_de_Versailles%2C_Rond-Poin